# Theming with CSS Variables

## Variable Naming

Use semantic names, not colors:

```css
/* ✅ Good - semantic */
--bg-primary
--text-muted
--accent-primary

/* ❌ Bad - color names */
--dark-gray
--blue
```

## Core Variables

Always use these variables instead of hardcoded colors:

| Variable | Usage |
|----------|-------|
| `--bg-primary` | Main background |
| `--bg-secondary` | Cards, inputs |
| `--bg-tertiary` | Hover states |
| `--text-primary` | Main text |
| `--text-secondary` | Secondary text |
| `--text-muted` | Muted/label text |
| `--border-primary` | Borders |
| `--accent-primary` | Buttons, highlights |

## Usage

```css
/* ✅ Good */
.card {
  background: var(--bg-secondary);
  color: var(--text-primary);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-primary);
}

/* ❌ Bad - hardcoded colors */
.card {
  background: #2a2a2a;
  color: #f0f0f0;
}
```

## Light Mode

Variables are redefined in `@media (prefers-color-scheme: light)`.
No additional code needed - just use the variables.
